# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# devinfra: machine-local state, generated secrets and per-host config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything under data/, envars/ and clients/ is provisioned per machine and is
# never tracked. One exception keeps a fresh clone usable: the `*.example`
# templates, which are the tracked, fill-in-yourself versions.
#
# The `!<dir>/**/` negations are load-bearing: git will not descend into an
# excluded parent directory, so without them the file negations never match.

# data/ -- runtime state, database files, gateway config and its SQLite DBs
data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/*.example

# envars/ -- generated environment files; commit the *.example templates only
envars/**
!envars/**/
!envars/**/*.example

# clients/ -- per-machine client configs (filled-in copies of the templates)
clients/**
!clients/**/
!clients/**/*.example

# builds/forgejomcp/binaries/ -- upstream release object code, GPL-3.0-or-later
# (see THIRD-PARTY.md). Committing it would make this repository its distributor
# and bring GPL-3.0 §6, so it is fetched per checkout by scripts/pre-setup.sh
# instead, and the forgejomcp image build fails without it.
builds/forgejomcp/binaries/
